    <h1>About SkyPadel</h1>
    <p>One brand, obsessed with getting the bounce right.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container-fluid bg-3 about-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-sm-6">
        <h2>Why we started SkyPadel</h2>
        <p>SkyPadel started with a simple frustration: too many matches interrupted by a flat ball or an empty tube. We set out to build one brand of padel and tennis balls that plays exactly the same, tube after tube, case after case &mdash; and sell it in bundles that match how people actually play, from a casual weekend rally to a full club season.</p>
        <p>No confusing lineup of competing brands and grades. Just one dependable ball, in the sizes that make sense.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-sm-6">
        <h2>What we stand for</h2>
        <ul class="about-list">
          <li><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-ok"></span> Consistent, match-ready bounce in every tube</li>
          <li><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-ok"></span> Durable felt and rubber built to last the rally</li>
          <li><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-ok"></span> Straightforward bundle pricing &mdash; buy more, pay less per ball</li>
          <li><span class="glyphicon glyphicon-ok"></span> Reliable stock for players, coaches and clubs alike</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row about-stats">
      <div class="col-sm-4 text-center">
        <div class="ball-graphic ball-padel about-stat-ball"></div>
        <h3>Padel Balls</h3>
        <p>Tuned for control on indoor and outdoor courts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-sm-4 text-center">
        <div class="ball-graphic ball-tennis about-stat-ball"></div>
        <h3>Tennis Balls</h3>
        <p>Reliable pressure and bounce, match after match.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col-sm-4 text-center">
